From a13c85d6c3709f8da5468b35f077e024130280d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:45:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Widen operands before multiplications assigned to larger
 types

CodeQL cpp/integer-multiplication-cast-to-long: these products were
computed in 32-bit int/unsigned and only then widened to size_t or
uint64_t, so large dimensions (e.g. image or texture sizes from decoded
files) could wrap before the allocation size is computed. Widen the
first operand so the multiplication itself is done in the destination
type.

In GUIPanelContainer the result is assigned back to an int, so convert
m_items.size() to int instead of promoting the rest to unsigned long.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

[Hades: the hunk of xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/streams/RetroPlayerAudio.cpp
is the same one-line change, made where the line is in this tree: Piers
commit cdecc111ecd1 rewrote the code around it.]
